[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: One devenv task renders a root: export, view-check, wireline, render

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-VIEW-TASK
TITLE: One devenv task renders a root: export, view-check, wireline, render
DEPTH: interface-settled
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
devenv tasks run --mode before view:render --input root=UID runs the
strictdoc export into a clean directory, the view check, the wireline and
the renderer, and leaves the page and the payload under output/view/, which
is gitignored: the canon is the source and the page is regenerable. Flipping
the view is passing a different root. The root travels through devenv's
task-input channel, because devenv tasks run has no argument passthrough. A
view-check finding does not stop the render: the findings are in the payload
and on the page's start screen; a bad root does. The published artifact is a
copy of that page, republished by hand or by a task, never edited.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The task is the only sanctioned way to regenerate (the repo's generate:* convention); a page nobody can regenerate is the one-off render again.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Built 2026-08-30 in dev/tasks/generate.nix, beside the generate:* tasks.
The statement first read "-- --root UID"; measured that day, devenv tasks
run reads a "-- --root X" as a task named "--root" and refuses it, so the
root goes through --input root=UID and the task reads it from
DEVENV_TASK_INPUT. Measured wall time for --input root=NAR-SEMANTIC-LAYER:
about 19 s, of which devenv's own evaluation is the bulk.
<<<
